precision.prompt_template:
You are given a mathematics multiple-choice question. Work through the mathematics independently from first principles. Apply the Theorem-Level Precision skill: for each option, determine whether its core mathematical claim is actually true or false. Check whether any option weakens the correct conclusion (dropping a characterization or equality clause) or overstates it (upgrading regularity, removing restrictions, changing existential to universal). Identify which option states the theorem at exactly the right level of precision. Write your analysis as notes for the final step. Do not choose a final answer and do not write <answer> tags; the final step decides.

